    "answer": {
      "short": "The angles are not formed by the same two intersecting straight lines. $d=151^\\circ$.",
      "worked": "$d$ is not vertically opposite $116^\\circ$ because the angles are not formed by the same two intersecting straight lines.\nAngles at a point add to $360^\\circ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}d+71+116+22&=360\\\\d+209&=360\\\\d&=151\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $d=151^\\circ$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
